// F27 EINF-TOPOLOGY SUCCESSOR (R3) -- WOMERSLEY PULSATILE PIPE, BUTTERFLY O-GRID.
// SAME OUTER WALL, SAME (NC, NR, NZ), SAME CORE_FRAC = 0.5, SAME (1 1 1) grading
// as the frozen parent blockMeshDict.template.  THE ONE CHANGE: the core/ring
// block interface is a CIRCULAR ARC (a ROUNDED SQUARE), not a straight square.
// The frozen parent left the interface as a square whose four corners sit at
// r = CORE_FRAC*R = 0.5, theta = 45/135/225/315 deg; those four sharp
// block-interface corners are the geometric feature that aliases the D4 corner
// mode measured by G-F27R-2 (Einf) at R2 (GATE FAIL, order 1.272, support 0.23%
// of cells at the core/ring corner).  The interface is re-shaped to the
// AREA-EQUIVALENT CIRCLE of the frozen square core: the square core has corners
// at r=0.5, side 2*(0.5/sqrt2)=0.70710678, area exactly 0.5; the circle of the
// same area has radius sqrt(0.5/pi) = 0.5*sqrt(2/pi) = 0.3989422804014327.  This
// is an AREA-PRESERVING reshape (the minimal one): it keeps the core's
// cross-sectional area identical while distributing it as a disk, softening the
// four corners and making the ring a near-orthogonal annulus.  The bulge radius
// is a GEOMETRIC principle independent of any solved value AND of the non-ortho
// metric (checkMesh confirms it also nearly minimises max non-orthogonality:
// 19.1/24.1/27.0 deg vs the frozen square's 28.6/36.2/40.4).  A FULL circle
// (r=0.5) was BUILT and REJECTED: it fails MESH_STANDARD 3.1 (medium 71.6 deg,
// fine 80.6 deg > 70) and the volume-ratio bound (fine 17.1 > 8) by over-
// distorting the core corner -- the classic reason butterfly cores are rounded
// squares, not full circles.
//
// WHY THE BAND IS BYTE-IDENTICAL.  The band rests on A_MESH (the built mesh's own
// cross-sectional area, via exact_f27.r_eff_of) and on MODEL_NR / STEPS.  A_MESH
// is the area bounded by the OUTER WALL only; the core/ring interface is an
// INTERNAL boundary and reshaping it does not change the union core+ring = the
// region inside the wall.  NC, NR, NZ, CORE_FRAC and the wall arcs are unchanged,
// so MODEL_NR, STEPS and A_MESH are unchanged -> predictions() and both bands are
// byte-identical.  Only W_REF_MESH (a REPORTED-NOT-GATED reference, the
// volume-weighted mean of the exact axial velocity over the mesh's own cells)
// moves, because the interior cell distribution changes; it is re-registered in
// exact_f27_r3.py and pinned by build_f27_r3.py.  W_REF_MESH enters NO band.
//
// EVERY BLOCK IS `simpleGrading (1 1 1)` -- NO grading parameter anywhere
// (MESH_STANDARD 9.2 read-back holds unchanged).  The interface arc is an `edges`
// entry, not a grading multiplier.  Cross-section cells = nc^2 + 4 nc nr; total
// = that x nz, unchanged from the frozen parent at every level.
